## Metric formulas

nucleo-metodologia-formula-crypto_tvl = TVL of the network's protocols (DefiLlama), in reais at the PTAX rate; networks only (layer 1 and 2)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-crypto_watchlist_users = CoinGecko users with the asset on their watchlist or portfolio (a proxy for adoption)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-crypto_active_addresses = Average active addresses per day over 30 days (Coin Metrics, open Community API, CC BY-NC 4.0); networks outside the open API have no data
nucleo-metodologia-formula-crypto_fdv_to_mcap = Fully diluted valuation ÷ market cap (above 3 = a lot of supply still to be released)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-crypto_supply_inflation = Growth of the circulating supply over 12 months (market cap ÷ price, CoinGecko history)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-crypto_supply_emitted = Circulating supply ÷ maximum supply (no maximum supply: not applicable, inflation is used)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-crypto_holder_concentration = Share of the supply held by the 10 largest wallets, excluding exchanges and contracts
nucleo-metodologia-formula-crypto_unlocks = Supply to be unlocked in the next 12 months ÷ circulating supply; proof-of-work coins (CoinGecko categories) have no allocations to unlock (0). Tokens: schedules are only in paid services (Token Unlocks, Messari), so the metric has no data
nucleo-metodologia-formula-crypto_market_cap = Circulating supply × price (CoinGecko or DefiLlama), in reais at the PTAX rate
nucleo-metodologia-formula-crypto_rank = Market cap ranking on CoinGecko (top 20 = lower risk of disappearing)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-crypto_volume = Volume traded in the last 24 hours (CoinGecko), in reais at the PTAX rate
nucleo-metodologia-formula-crypto_turnover = 24-hour volume ÷ market cap (very low = illiquid; very high = speculative)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-crypto_age_years = Years since the genesis block (CoinGecko); a history with no failure is the security measure available
nucleo-metodologia-formula-crypto_hacks = 100 − 50 per attack on the network itself (51%, forged proof, validator key…) in DefiLlama's list of hacks (`targetType` Chain, by the network's name); attacks on the network's protocols don't count
nucleo-metodologia-formula-crypto_nakamoto = Smallest number of validators or pools that controls more than 1/3 (PoS) or 1/2 (PoW) of the network; bitcoin only, from the week's blocks per mining pool (mempool.space); other networks have no free source
nucleo-metodologia-formula-crypto_commits_4w = Commits to the main repository in the last 4 weeks (CoinGecko, GitHub data)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-crypto_github_stars = Stars of the main repository (CoinGecko, GitHub data)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-crypto_volatility = Standard deviation of the daily returns over 12 months × √(observations per year) (the app's prices; without them, DefiLlama's prices in dollars)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-crypto_max_drawdown = Largest drop from the previous peak in the last 12 months
nucleo-metodologia-formula-crypto_ath_drawdown = 1 − price ÷ all-time high in dollars (CoinGecko)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-stable_backing = Score of the declared backing mechanism (DefiLlama: fiat currency, crypto, algorithmic); table in classes/crypto.json
nucleo-metodologia-formula-stable_attestation = Frequency and quality of the attestations (full audit = best)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-stable_max_deviation = Largest |price ÷ peg − 1| in the daily closes in dollars over the last 12 months
nucleo-metodologia-formula-stable_depeg_days = Share of the days in the last 12 months with a deviation above 0.5%
nucleo-metodologia-formula-stable_mean_deviation = Average of |price ÷ peg − 1| over the last 12 months
nucleo-metodologia-formula-stable_regulation = Regulated issuer (MiCA, NYDFS, e-money license) = best
nucleo-metodologia-formula-roic = NOPAT ÷ (net debt + shareholders' equity), NOPAT = EBIT × (1 − 34%)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-roe = Net income (12 months) ÷ average shareholders' equity
nucleo-metodologia-formula-gross_profitability = (Revenue − COGS) ÷ total assets
nucleo-metodologia-formula-ebit_margin = EBIT ÷ net revenue (12 months)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-net_margin = Net income ÷ net revenue (12 months)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-net_debt_ebitda = (Gross debt + leases − cash) ÷ EBITDA (12 months), EBITDA = EBIT + D&A recalculated from the statements
nucleo-metodologia-formula-interest_coverage = EBIT ÷ net financial expense (12 months)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-altman_z2 = 6.56·X1 + 3.26·X2 + 6.72·X3 + 1.05·X4 (X1 working capital/assets, X2 retained earnings/assets, X3 EBIT/assets, X4 book equity/liabilities)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-current_ratio = Current assets ÷ current liabilities
nucleo-metodologia-formula-cash_to_st_debt = Cash and investments ÷ loans and borrowings in current liabilities
nucleo-metodologia-formula-fcf_margin = (CFO − capex) ÷ net revenue (12 months)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-fcf_to_net_income = (CFO − capex) ÷ net income (12 months); above 1 is good, very high values only mean a small profit
nucleo-metodologia-formula-accruals = (Net income − CFO) ÷ average total assets
nucleo-metodologia-formula-piotroski = Sum of 9 binary criteria (profitability, leverage/liquidity, efficiency) between the last two fiscal years
nucleo-metodologia-formula-revenue_cagr_5y_real = CAGR of annual net revenue over 5 years, net of the IPCA for the period
nucleo-metodologia-formula-eps_cagr_5y = CAGR of net income per share (income ÷ shares outstanding) over 5 fiscal years
nucleo-metodologia-formula-revenue_cagr_3y_real = CAGR of annual net revenue over 3 years, net of the IPCA for the period
nucleo-metodologia-formula-asset_growth = Total assets ÷ total assets 12 months earlier − 1 (Cooper, Gulen & Schill: aggressive expansion predicts lower returns)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-asset_turnover = Net revenue (12 months) ÷ average total assets
nucleo-metodologia-formula-cash_cycle_days = Days sales outstanding + days inventory outstanding − days payable outstanding (based on 12 months of revenue and COGS)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-earnings_yield = EBIT (12 months) ÷ (market cap + net debt + minority interests)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-fcf_yield = Free cash flow (12 months) ÷ market cap
nucleo-metodologia-formula-earnings_to_price = Net income (12 months) ÷ market cap
nucleo-metodologia-formula-pb = Market cap ÷ shareholders' equity
nucleo-metodologia-formula-ev_ebitda = (Market cap + net debt + minority interests) ÷ EBITDA (12 months)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-roe_stability = Standard deviation of the annual ROE over the last 5 to 10 fiscal years
nucleo-metodologia-formula-loss_years_10y = Fiscal years with negative net income in the last 10 (at least 3 fiscal years)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-volatility_1y = Standard deviation of the daily returns over 1 year × √252
nucleo-metodologia-formula-payout = Dividends and interest on equity declared (12 months) ÷ net income
nucleo-metodologia-formula-dividend_fcf_coverage = Free cash flow ÷ dividends and interest on equity paid (12 months)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-dilution = Shares outstanding ÷ shares 12 months earlier − 1 (negative = buyback)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-momentum_12_1 = Price 1 month ago ÷ price 12 months ago − 1
nucleo-metodologia-formula-rule_of_40 = Revenue growth over 12 months + free cash flow margin
nucleo-metodologia-formula-roic_norm = Average annual ROIC over the last 5 fiscal years (cyclical normalization)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-net_debt_ebitda_norm = (Gross debt + leases − cash) ÷ average EBITDA over the last 5 fiscal years
nucleo-metodologia-formula-roa = Net income (12 months) ÷ average total assets
nucleo-metodologia-formula-equity_to_assets = Shareholders' equity ÷ total assets
nucleo-metodologia-formula-net_income_growth = Net income over 12 months ÷ net income over the 12 months before − 1
nucleo-metodologia-formula-dy = Income per share over the last 12 months ÷ price
nucleo-metodologia-formula-etf_ter = The ETF's total expense ratio
nucleo-metodologia-formula-etf_tracking_diff = The ETF's return over 12 months − the benchmark index's return over the same period (ideally close to −fee)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-etf_tracking_error = Standard deviation of the daily differences between the ETF and the index, annualized (12 months)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-etf_avg_volume = Average traded value over the latest sessions (in reais; ETFs listed abroad converted at the PTAX rate)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-etf_aum = Net assets in CVM's registry of funds and classes
nucleo-metodologia-formula-etf_domicile = Score of the domicile for a Brazilian investor (withholding on dividends, Law 14,754/2023 regime); table in classes/funds.json
nucleo-metodologia-formula-etf_replication = Physical and transparent = best
nucleo-metodologia-formula-fund_age_years = Years since inception (CVM's registry of funds and classes); a proxy for the management track record
nucleo-metodologia-formula-etf_volatility = Standard deviation of the daily returns over 12 months × √(observations per year)
nucleo-metodologia-formula-etf_max_drawdown = Largest price drop from the previous peak, in a window of up to 36 months

## Why the metric has no data

nucleo-metodologia-indisponivel-crypto_holder_concentration = The distribution by wallet needs paid or key-based block explorers (Etherscan, Glassnode); there is no free structured source.
nucleo-metodologia-indisponivel-stable_attestation = Reserve attestations and audits are PDFs from the issuers; there is no free structured source.
nucleo-metodologia-indisponivel-stable_regulation = There is no free structured database of the issuers' licenses and regulation.
nucleo-metodologia-indisponivel-etf_ter = ETF fees only appear on the pages of B3 and of the fund managers (CVM doesn't publish the statements of index funds and Yahoo requires a session); there is no free structured source.
nucleo-metodologia-indisponivel-etf_replication = The replication method and securities lending are only in the fund rules and prospectuses (PDF); there is no free structured source.

## Red flags

nucleo-metodologia-flag-altman_distress = Altman Z'' in the distress zone
nucleo-metodologia-flag-beneish_manipulation = Beneish: likely earnings manipulation (review)
nucleo-metodologia-flag-piotroski_low = Very low Piotroski score
nucleo-metodologia-flag-interest_coverage_low = Interest coverage below 1.5x for 2 quarters
nucleo-metodologia-flag-fcf_negative_3y = Negative free cash flow for 3 years in a row
nucleo-metodologia-flag-dividends_above_fcf = Dividends above free cash flow for 2 years or more
nucleo-metodologia-flag-dilution_high = Dilution above 5% a year
nucleo-metodologia-flag-negative_equity = Negative shareholders' equity
nucleo-metodologia-flag-dsri_high = Receivables growing much faster than revenue (DSRI)
nucleo-metodologia-flag-low_liquidity = Low liquidity (average volume below R$ 1 million a day)
nucleo-metodologia-flag-etf_low_liquidity = Low liquidity (average volume below R$ 1 million a day)
nucleo-metodologia-flag-etf_small_aum = Small ETF (assets below R$ 100 million)
nucleo-metodologia-flag-crypto_high_fdv = A lot of supply still to be released (FDV above 3× the market cap)
nucleo-metodologia-flag-crypto_small_cap = Small market cap (below R$ 1 billion)
nucleo-metodologia-flag-stable_depeg = Lost its peg by more than 3% in the last 12 months
nucleo-metodologia-flag-stable_algorithmic = Algorithmic stablecoin (no reserves)

